- Upgrade dep @confluentinc/kafka-javascript from 1.9.1 to 1.10.0
- Do not insert (or overwrite) in NGSI sinks `recvtime` when is providead a measure (#299)
- Fix: historic sink no longer requires `TimeInstant` on the record. Changed `pk.mode` to `none` in the historic JDBC sink (plain insert, no PK needed) and made the Kafka message key's `timeinstant` field optional in kafnus-ngsi when the entity does not carry one, instead of always requiring it (#304)
- Add: split historic entities by per-attribute metadata TimeInstant so each observation time is written as its own row, gated by the global KAFNUS_NGSI_SPLIT_BY_TIMEINSTANT flag (default off) (#294)
- Add: KAFNUS_NGSI_ENSURE_TIMEINSTANT flag (default off) to guarantee historic and mutable rows always have a usable `timeinstant`, resolving it from attribute metadata / entity-level TimeInstant / `recvtime` and overriding a stale value if needed; independent of and composable with KAFNUS_NGSI_SPLIT_BY_TIMEINSTANT (#294)
- Add: `requires_env.json` to end2end tests to configure specific env variable settings for different test cases other than defaults